	(text "for 20-30V RTD:\ndivider: ( 27^-1 + (27*2)^-1 )^-1 = (.05555)^-1 = 18\n\n0.1524 = 18/118 = multiplier on input voltage to 4V RTD\n\n0.0762 = 18/118 /2 = multipler on input voltage to 2V RTD\n\nSo, on 20-30V:\n4V RTD: 3.05V - 4.58V.\n2V RTD: 1.52V - 2.29V.\n\n4V RTD turns contactor on at 2V, so 1V 2V RTD is digital high."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
